# Line endings of files that are generated, or compared or checksummed by a tool, are
# fixed to LF, so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true does not change them:
# - openapi.json: written by `pnpm openapi:generate`, checked by `pnpm openapi:check`.
# - pnpm-lock.yaml: written by pnpm.
# - prisma/migrations: Prisma checksums each applied migration; a changed line ending
#   reads as an edited migration.
# - lint-fixtures: `pnpm lint:rules` runs ESLint (and Prettier) over them.
# - docker: shell scripts run inside Linux containers.
# - .husky: git hook scripts run by sh, which a carriage return breaks (Git Bash too).
openapi.json text eol=lf
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf
prisma/migrations/** text eol=lf
lint-fixtures/** text eol=lf
docker/** text eol=lf
.husky/** text eol=lf
